fixup: correct plist-regen prose (HIGH); promote to top-level section (MEDIUM); link followup (LOW)

Adversarial review caught the technical claim inverted: `brew services restart` does
regenerate the plist, but from the installed keg (under Cellar/), not from the tap's
current formula. `brew services` doesn't track the tap. So the right invariant is
'plist regenerates from the keg' — `brew reinstall` is needed to swap the keg first.

Also calls out the version-bump caveat: `brew upgrade` replaces the keg automatically
(plist follows), but a tap PR that changes the service block without a version bump
won't propagate via `brew update` (keg unchanged).

Promoted from a subsection under § Migration to its own top-level section so it stays
discoverable for non-migrating operators (every future tap service-block change).

Added a direct link to the followup roadmap item (`pd-doctor-detect-drift-between-live`)
in the doc body so the followup pointer survives the merge.

